<symbol type="16" id="56" code="302" name="Shallow body of water (A)&#13;"><description>An area of shallow water such as a pond, river or fountain that can be crossed. The body of water should be less than 0.5 m deep and runnable.
If the body of water is not runnable it shall be represented with the symbol Uncrossable body of water (301). If no other line symbol touches the border of the passable body of water, the border shall be represented with a blue line.
Minimum width: 0.3 mm
Minimum area (inside): 0.5 mm² (footprint 8 m²)</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="57"/><part symbol="58"/></combined_symbol>
